ion. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}]}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}],"name":"color"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-sound type is used for bend and slide elements, and is similar to the trill-sound attribute group. Here the beats element refers to the number of discrete elements (like MIDI pitch bends) used to represent a continuous bend or slide. The first-beat indicates the percentage of the duration for starting a bend; the last-beat the percentage for ending it. The default choices are:"}]}],"name":"bendSound"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineKind":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineKind","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineKind"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The line-type type distinguishes between solid, dashed, dotted, and wavy lines."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLLineKind","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinekind","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineKind"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlide/init(id:value:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:bendSound:)":{"